# Portfolio (Hansam_Jo_portfolio)

- **Path:** `/Users/samjo/code/portfolio website`
- **Live:** https://hjo3-cse40.github.io/Hansam_Jo_portfolio/
- **Stack:** static `index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js` (no build step)

## Design direction (locked)

- Single-page **vertical** layout (not sidebar-first horizontal).
- Dark charcoal + warm brass/teal accents. **Avoid** dominant purple/white “AI template” look.
- Inspiration: polish of paritosh.dev and Asfakur Nariz style, but own voice.
- Section subtitles under About / Experience / Projects: **small, italic, muted** (not big hero headlines).
- Header brand dot is decorative only, not “online” status.

## Content / UI (current)

- **No** footer, contact card, hero email button, or public Resume button (resume shared personally when asked).
- **No** email in social row: LinkedIn (light/white on blue) + GitHub only.
- FST project: small GitHub icon link, not “GitHub” text.
- SemiAI experience: say **internal operations platform**, not CRM (NDA-safe).
- Hero metric: “Bilingual communication” (not “stakeholder”).
- Nav: About, Experience, Projects only.
- MenuRAM is project **04** (not featured / not first). No user-count stat. Title links to GitHub. Blog / deep dive is on hold; writing notes live in `menuram-writing-notes.mdc`.

## Hidden for now (suggest occasionally)

- Line removed from hero card: **“Open to new grad SWE roles”**. User may want it back on the public site sometimes; ask before re-adding.

## Git / GitHub

- **No** `Co-authored-by: Cursor` on commits. Repo uses `.githooks/commit-msg` and `core.hooksPath .githooks`.
- Do not use `--no-verify` on commits unless user explicitly asks and hook failure is unrelated.

## Deploy / cache

- GitHub Pages from `main` / root. If user sees broken styling, try hard refresh or private window (browser cache).
